#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# alternating_harmonic_number

#% text
# `alternating_harmonic_number(m)` gives the sum of (-1)^(k + 1)/k for k = 1, ..., m.

#% text
# `alternating_harmonic_number(m, r)` gives the sum of (-1)^(k + 1)/k^r; `alternating_harmonic_number(m, r, s)` the sum of (-1)^(k + 1) s^k/k^r.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# At m = inf the values are `log(2)`, `(1 - 2^(1 - r)) zeta(r)` and `-polylog(r, -s)`.

#% item
# At inexact m the tail is written with the Hurwitz zeta function (the digamma function for r = 1), so the function is continued to real and complex m.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
table(alternating_harmonic_number(k), [k, 8])
#% output
#= [1, 1/2, 5/6, 7/12, 47/60, 37/60, 319/420, 533/840]

#% cell
alternating_harmonic_number(4, r)
#% output
#= 1 - 2^-r - 4^-r + 3^-r

#% cell
n(alternating_harmonic_number(3, 5, 1/2), 30)
#% output
#= 0.4927019032921810699588477366255144

#% cell
alternating_harmonic_number(inf, r)
#% output
#= (1 - 2^(1 - r))*zeta(r)

#% cell
alternating_harmonic_number(2.5)
#% output
#= 0.6931471805599453 - 0.16253700653843667im

